### Bubble Sort
Bubble Sort is simple to understand and implement but is not efficient for large data sets. It repeatedly steps through the list, compares adjacent elements, and swaps them if they are in the wrong order.

```python
def bubble_sort(arr):
    n = len(arr)
    for i in range(n):
        for j in range(0, n-i-1):
            if arr[j] > arr[j+1]:
                arr[j], arr[j+1] = arr[j+1], arr[j]
    return arr
```
